# The item fixtures are CONTENT-ADDRESSED: item.load hashes the bytes of everything under
# files/ and record.admit refuses any run record whose digest disagrees. Line-ending
# translation would therefore make the item's identity MACHINE-DEPENDENT - a record
# produced on Linux would be unadmittable on Windows, and the failure would read as "a
# record from a different item" rather than as a checkout artefact.
#
# -text: store and check out the bytes verbatim, on every platform.
* -text
